1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Everyone blames winter for this.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Summer is what actually kills your battery.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Heat cooks the acid and corrodes
the plates all season, quietly.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Then one cool morning,
there's nothing left to give.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Slow crank. Dim headlights at idle.
One jump start already.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Most batteries last three to five years —
heat cuts that shorter.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before it strands you.
